IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-14.l4 -- ARTICLE 14 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: INFORMATION TO BE PROVIDED WHERE PERSONAL DATA HAVE NOT BEEN
-- OBTAINED FROM THE DATA SUBJECT (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 179-205 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the two heading lines of
-- Article 14 at 179-180 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE `Duty outcome` for every duty with a gate, MAYBE BOOLEAN for
-- the exceptions of paragraph 5, a NUMBER (the months allowed by paragraph 3), a DEONTIC for each regulative rule.
--
-- WHOSE.  The controller owes the information; the data subject may rely on it.
-- THE LISTS and the item-by-item reading are the same as in P2-art-13.l4: the caller states the items PROVIDED and the
-- items the data subject ALREADY HAS (paragraph 5(a), "where and insofar as the data subject already has the information").
-- THE EXCEPTIONS OF PARAGRAPH 5(b) TO (d) are asked once, as `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4`
-- (MAYBE BOOLEAN), and paragraphs 1, 2 and 4 take that answer as an input: JUST TRUE means the paragraphs do not apply.
-- THE CLOCK of a regulative rule counts months from the moment the personal data are obtained (paragraph 3).
-- READING A RESULT (NOTES).  NOTHING means the Regulation does not answer on these facts; never read it as no.
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 14(1) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller`
    `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative`
    `Art 14(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer`
    `Art 14(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended`
    `Art 14(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing`
    `Art 14(1)(d) the categories of personal data concerned`
    `Art 14(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data`
    `Art 14(1)(f) the intended transfer to a recipient in a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards`

DECLARE `Art 14(2) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `Art 14(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period`
    `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`
    `Art 14(2)(c) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability`
    `Art 14(2)(d) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal`
    `Art 14(2)(e) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority`
    `Art 14(2)(f) the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources`
    `Art 14(2)(g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences`

DECLARE `Art 14 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 14(1) and (2) provide the data subject with the information that paragraphs 1 and 2 list`
    `Art 14(4) provide the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information`
    `Art 14(5)(b) take appropriate measures to protect the data subject's rights and freedoms and legitimate interests, including making the information publicly available`

§ `Article 14(1): the information where the data have not been obtained from the data subject`

-- src:181 | 1. Where personal data have not been obtained from the data subject, the controller shall provide the data subject with the following information:
-- src:182 | (a) the identity and the contact details of the controller and, where applicable, of the controller's representative;
-- src:183 | (b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable;
-- src:184 | (c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended as well as the legal basis for the processing;
-- src:185 | (d) the categories of personal data concerned;
-- src:186 | (e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any;
-- src:187 | (f) where applicable, that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a recipient in a third country or international organisation and the existence or absence of an adequacy decision by the Commission, or in the case of transfers referred to in Article 46 or 47, or the second subparagraph of Article 49(1), reference to the appropriate or suitable safeguards and the means to obtain a copy of them or where they have been made available.
@ref Art 14(1) chapeau and points (a) to (f) (src:181-187)
GIVEN `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the controller has a representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has designated a data protection officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a recipient in a third country or international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items of information that the controller provides` IS A LIST OF `Art 14(1) item of information`
      `the items of information that the data subject already has` IS A LIST OF `Art 14(1) item of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 14(1) the controller provides the data subject with the following information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where personal data have not been obtained from the data subject"
        IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1 to 4 shall not apply where and insofar as"
        IF NOT (    held `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller`
                AND held `Art 14(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended`
                AND held `Art 14(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing`
                AND held `Art 14(1)(d) the categories of personal data concerned`
                AND (IF `the controller has a representative` THEN held `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `the controller has designated a data protection officer` THEN held `Art 14(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` THEN held `Art 14(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a recipient in a third country or international organisation` THEN held `Art 14(1)(f) the intended transfer to a recipient in a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards` ELSE TRUE))
        THEN IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller shall provide the data subject with the following information"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the answer of paragraph 5 is not given, since an item is missing and paragraph 5 may take the duty away
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is met`
    WHERE
        held item MEANS elem item `the items of information that the controller provides` OR elem item `the items of information that the data subject already has`

§ `Article 14(2): the further information`

-- src:188 | 2. In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1, the controller shall provide the data subject with the following information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing in respect of the data subject:
-- src:189 | (a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or if that is not possible, the criteria used to determine that period;
-- src:190 | (b) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1), the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party;
-- src:191 | (c) the existence of the right to request from the controller access to and rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing concerning the data subject and to object to processing as well as the right to data portability;
-- src:192 | (d) where processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2), the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal;
-- src:193 | (e) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority;
-- src:194 | (f) from which source the personal data originate, and if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources;
-- src:195 | (g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4) and, at least in those cases, meaningful information about the logic involved, as well as the significance and the envisaged consequences of such processing for the data subject.
@ref Art 14(2) chapeau and points (a) to (g) (src:188-195)
GIVEN `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items of further information that the controller provides` IS A LIST OF `Art 14(2) item of information`
      `the items of further information that the data subject already has` IS A LIST OF `Art 14(2) item of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 14(2) the controller provides the data subject with the following information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1": paragraph 1 is the case of data not obtained from the data subject, and the pointer has no gate word (ruling (c); fork F14-1)
        IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1 to 4 shall not apply where and insofar as"
        IF NOT (    held `Art 14(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period`
                AND held `Art 14(2)(c) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability`
                AND held `Art 14(2)(e) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority`
                AND held `Art 14(2)(f) the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources`
                AND (IF `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN held `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` THEN held `Art 14(2)(d) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` ELSE TRUE)
                AND (IF `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` THEN held `Art 14(2)(g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` ELSE TRUE))
        THEN IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller shall provide the data subject with the following information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing in respect of the data subject"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the answer of paragraph 5 is not given
        IF `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS NOTHING
           AND NOT (held `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether item (b) is owed ("where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1)") is P1's answer, and it does not answer on these facts; every other item that applies has been provided
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is met`
    WHERE
        held item MEANS elem item `the items of further information that the controller provides` OR elem item `the items of further information that the data subject already has`
    -- (d) "where processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)", (g) "the existence of automated decision-making ... referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)" and (f) "if applicable": required only where the caller states the fact; (g) "at least in those cases" is read as in Article 13(2) (fork F13-3).

§ `Article 14(1) and (2): one item at a time`

-- As in P2-art-13.l4: the two functions below ask whether ONE item named by the caller is owed (R10).
-- JUST TRUE: owed.  JUST FALSE: the text says it is not (a failed "where", a condition that fails, paragraph 5).  NOTHING: P1's answer (Article 6(1)(f), paragraph 5) is missing.
-- src:181 | 1. Where personal data have not been obtained from the data subject, the controller shall provide the data subject with the following information:
-- src:182 | (a) the identity and the contact details of the controller and, where applicable, of the controller's representative;
-- src:183 | (b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable;
-- src:184 | (c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended as well as the legal basis for the processing;
-- src:185 | (d) the categories of personal data concerned;
-- src:186 | (e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any;
-- src:187 | (f) where applicable, that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a recipient in a third country or international organisation and the existence or absence of an adequacy decision by the Commission, or in the case of transfers referred to in Article 46 or 47, or the second subparagraph of Article 49(1), reference to the appropriate or suitable safeguards and the means to obtain a copy of them or where they have been made available.
@ref Art 14(1) item by item (chapeau and points (a) to (f)) (src:181-187)
GIVEN `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      item IS AN `Art 14(1) item of information`
      `the controller has a representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has designated a data protection officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a recipient in a third country or international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject already has the item of information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(1) the controller owes the data subject the item of information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where personal data have not been obtained from the data subject"
        IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1 to 4 shall not apply where and insofar as"
        IF `the data subject already has the item of information`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "5. Paragraphs 1 to 4 shall not apply where and insofar as: (a) the data subject already has the information"
        IF NOT (applies item)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b)): "(a) ... where applicable, of the controller's representative", "(b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable", "(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any", "(f) where applicable, that the controller intends to transfer personal data": the item is not owed where its condition fails
        IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph 5 takes the duty away is the answer of `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) ...`, and it does not answer on these facts
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        applies i MEANS
            CONSIDER i
            WHEN `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` THEN `the controller has a representative`
            WHEN `Art 14(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer` THEN `the controller has designated a data protection officer`
            WHEN `Art 14(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` THEN `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data`
            WHEN `Art 14(1)(f) the intended transfer to a recipient in a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards` THEN `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a recipient in a third country or international organisation`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:188 | 2. In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1, the controller shall provide the data subject with the following information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing in respect of the data subject:
-- src:189 | (a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or if that is not possible, the criteria used to determine that period;
-- src:190 | (b) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1), the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party;
-- src:191 | (c) the existence of the right to request from the controller access to and rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing concerning the data subject and to object to processing as well as the right to data portability;
-- src:192 | (d) where processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2), the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal;
-- src:193 | (e) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority;
-- src:194 | (f) from which source the personal data originate, and if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources;
-- src:195 | (g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4) and, at least in those cases, meaningful information about the logic involved, as well as the significance and the envisaged consequences of such processing for the data subject.
@ref Art 14(2) item by item (chapeau and points (a) to (g)) (src:188-195)
GIVEN `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      item IS AN `Art 14(2) item of information`
      `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject already has the item of information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(2) the controller owes the data subject the item of information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1": paragraph 1 is the case of data not obtained from the data subject, and the pointer has no gate word (ruling (c); fork F14-1)
        IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1 to 4 shall not apply where and insofar as"
        IF `the data subject already has the item of information`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "5. Paragraphs 1 to 4 shall not apply where and insofar as: (a) the data subject already has the information"
        IF item EQUALS `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`
           AND `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether item (b) is owed ("where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1)") is P1's answer, and it does not answer on these facts
        IF NOT (applies item)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b)): "(b) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1)", "(d) where processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)", "(g) the existence of automated decision-making ... referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)": the item is not owed where its condition fails
        IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph 5 takes the duty away is the answer of `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) ...`, and it does not answer on these facts
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        applies i MEANS
            CONSIDER i
            WHEN `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` THEN `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            WHEN `Art 14(2)(d) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` THEN `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)`
            WHEN `Art 14(2)(g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` THEN `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `Article 14(3): when the information is to be provided`

-- src:196 | 3. The controller shall provide the information referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2:
-- src:197 | (a) within a reasonable period after obtaining the personal data, but at the latest within one month, having regard to the specific circumstances in which the personal data are processed;
-- src:198 | (b) if the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject, at the latest at the time of the first communication to that data subject; or
-- src:199 | (c) if a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged, at the latest when the personal data are first disclosed.
@ref Art 14(3) chapeau and points (a) to (c): the months allowed (src:196-199)
GIVEN `the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` IS A NUMBER
      `a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 14(3) the months within which the information is to be provided` MEANS
    LET afterCommunication MEANS (IF `the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject` AND `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` LESS THAN 1 THEN `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` ELSE 1)
    IN IF `a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged` AND `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure` LESS THAN afterCommunication
       THEN `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure`
       ELSE afterCommunication
    -- the earliest of the applicable limits: (a) at the latest within one month, (b) at the latest at the time of the first communication, (c) at the latest when the data are first disclosed; the three are read as cumulative (fork F14-2)

-- src:196 | 3. The controller shall provide the information referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2:
-- src:197 | (a) within a reasonable period after obtaining the personal data, but at the latest within one month, having regard to the specific circumstances in which the personal data are processed;
-- src:198 | (b) if the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject, at the latest at the time of the first communication to that data subject; or
-- src:199 | (c) if a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged, at the latest when the personal data are first disclosed.
@ref Art 14(3) chapeau and points (a) to (c): provided in time (src:196-199)
GIVEN `the information is provided within a reasonable period after obtaining the personal data, having regard to the specific circumstances in which the personal data are processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to providing the information` IS A NUMBER
      `the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` IS A NUMBER
      `a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(3) the controller provides the information referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2 within the time that paragraph 3 requires` MEANS
    IF `the information is provided within a reasonable period after obtaining the personal data, having regard to the specific circumstances in which the personal data are processed`
       AND `the months from obtaining the personal data to providing the information` AT MOST (`Art 14(3) the months within which the information is to be provided` `the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject` `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` `a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged` `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "The controller shall provide the information referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2: (a) within a reasonable period after obtaining the personal data, but at the latest within one month"
    -- "reasonable": an undefined term; a plain fact the caller states.

GIVEN `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` IS A NUMBER
      `a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 14 action`
`Art 14(1) and (2) the controller must provide the data subject with the information within the time that Art 14(3) requires` MEANS
    IF `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` AND NOT (`Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 14(1) and (2) provide the data subject with the information that paragraphs 1 and 2 list`
         WITHIN (`Art 14(3) the months within which the information is to be provided` `the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject` `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` `a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged` `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the information was not provided within the time that Article 14(3) requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the clock counts months from the moment the personal data are obtained

§ `Article 14(4): further processing for another purpose`

-- src:200 | 4. Where the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were obtained, the controller shall provide the data subject prior to that further processing with information on that other purpose and with any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2.
@ref Art 14(4) (src:200)
GIVEN `the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the controller provided information on that other purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller provided any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was provided prior to that further processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject already has the information on that other purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject already has the relevant further information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 14(4) the controller provides the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were obtained`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were obtained"
        IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1 to 4 shall not apply where and insofar as"
        IF (`the controller provided information on that other purpose` OR `the data subject already has the information on that other purpose`)
           AND (`the controller provided any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2` OR `the data subject already has the relevant further information`)
           AND (`the information was provided prior to that further processing` OR (`the data subject already has the information on that other purpose` AND `the data subject already has the relevant further information`))
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE IF `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller shall provide the data subject prior to that further processing with information on that other purpose and with any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the answer of paragraph 5 is not given

GIVEN `the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the time at which the further processing is to begin` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 14 action`
`Art 14(4) the controller must provide the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information` MEANS
    IF `the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were obtained` AND NOT (`Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 14(4) provide the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information`
         WITHIN `the time at which the further processing is to begin`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the information was not provided prior to the further processing"
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- as in Article 13(3): the limit is the instant at which the further processing is to begin (fork F13-2)

§ `Article 14(5): where and insofar as paragraphs 1 to 4 do not apply`

